---
import SubpageLayout from '../../layouts/SubpageLayout.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import Tiles from '../../components/Tiles.astro';
const faqs = [
  { q: 'What is in-home care insurance billing?', a: 'Billing visits delivered in a home, clinic, or school under the correct place of service, with site enrollment where the payer requires it. Telehealth-only vendors often refuse the model. Anvil bills it: place of service, site enrollment, interventional psychiatry, and school-based programs.' },
  { q: 'Telehealth-only vendors turned us down. Why can you take us?', a: 'Because the platform was built for these models from the start. Place of service, facility components, travel, and site-specific enrollment are part of how we bill, not exceptions to it.' },
  { q: 'Does the rented PC work for in-person care?', a: 'Yes, where the state and payer allow the structure and the site is enrolled. Some in-person programs need site-level enrollment under your own PC sooner, and we sequence that first.' },
  { q: 'How does interventional psychiatry billing work?', a: 'TMS, ketamine and esketamine, plus the authorization and documentation those codes require. Facility and professional components can be two claims on one visit.' },
  { q: 'How does school-based program billing work?', a: 'Medicaid school-based billing, place of service 03, and the district agreements around it. We sequence site enrollment before volume moves.' },
];
---
<SubpageLayout
  metaTitle="Insurance billing for hybrid and in-home care"
  title="Hybrid, in-home, and in-person. The models telehealth vendors cannot bill."
  description="In-home care insurance billing for hybrid programs: place of service billing, site enrollment, interventional psychiatry, and school-based billing."
  eyebrow="Solutions / Hybrid and in-person"
  sub="In-home care insurance billing is what telehealth-only vendors refuse. If you deliver care in a clinic, a home, or a school, we bill it: place of service, site enrollment, interventional psychiatry, school-based programs."
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Solutions', path: '/solutions/hybrid-care' }, { name: 'Hybrid and in-person', path: '/solutions/hybrid-care' }]}
  faqs={faqs}
  ctaTitle="Describe your care model. We will tell you how it bills."
  ctaBody="Sites, states, license mix, and codes. We come back with the enrollment sequence and what runs on rental versus your own PC first."
  ctaPrimary={{ label: 'Get started', href: '/contact?src=hybrid' }}
>
  <Section eyebrow="What changes off-screen" title="Place of service billing and site enrollment">
    <p class="lede">Place of service billing is why hybrid claims fail on a telehealth-only stack. Each site is enrolled with each payer. Sequence matters. We enroll sites under your own PC when rental cannot cover them.</p>
    <Tiles items={[
      { icon: 'map', title: 'Place of service and site enrollment', body: 'POS 02, 10, 11, 12, and 03 are not interchangeable. Site enrollment is a payer file, not a checkbox on the claim.' },
      { icon: 'file', title: 'Facility and professional components', body: 'IOP, PHP, interventional procedures. Two claims, two fee schedules, one visit.' },
      { icon: 'users', title: 'In-home and school-based', body: 'Travel, place of service 12 and 03, district agreements, Medicaid school-based programs.' },
      { icon: 'shield', title: 'Authorizations', body: 'TMS, esketamine, ABA, and the re-authorization calendar that keeps a program from stalling.' },
    ]} cols={4} />
  </Section>
  <Section eyebrow="Specialty programs" title="Interventional psychiatry billing and school-based program billing">
    <div class="grid grid-2">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Interventional psychiatry billing</h3>
        <p class="muted">TMS, ketamine, and esketamine need authorizations, site enrollment, and often a facility component. We bill the professional and facility sides as the payer requires, then keep the re-authorization calendar from stalling the chair schedule.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>School-based program billing</h3>
        <p class="muted">Medicaid school-based programs need district agreements, place of service 03, and site enrollment before the first claim. We sequence that work so the school year is not waiting on a portal.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
</SubpageLayout>
